<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22944" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-dūresco</span></b> , rŭi,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
				n.</i>, <i>to become hard</i>, <i>to
				harden</i> (cf. percallesco; postAug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si vetus condyloma jam induruit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					6, 18, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grana,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 20, 2</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miles induruerat pro Vitellio,</span>”
				<i>had become unalterably firm in his attachment to
						Vitellius</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					3, 61</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in pravum,</span>”
				<i>to become hardened in</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 3, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
